;; Resident curator for the worldwide community-coverage corpus
;; (90-docs/community-coverage/ in com-junkawasaki, ADR-2607257200).
;;
;; This is the surface that actually drives the corpus. The LoopSpec sibling
;; (loops/community-coverage.edn) cannot tick it: a loop cycle opens a Radicle
;; issue, and :com-junkawasaki is a private organism whose issue authority is
;; :github-private — Radicle publication is refused by policy, correctly, since
;; the superproject is private. An ActorSpec run is mode :local (kotoba-code in
;; the declared project) and needs no Radicle repository.
;;
;; :actor/project is a dedicated clean worktree created OUTSIDE the superproject
;; per CLAUDE.md's parallel-agent rule; the superproject checkout itself is
;; permanently dirty with other sessions' work and can never be a cycle project.
{:actor/id :community-coverage/corpus-curator
 :actor/type :com-junkawasaki/community-coverage
 :actor/organism :com-junkawasaki
 :actor/project "/Users/junkawasaki/github/tamaki-workspaces/community-coverage"
 :actor/objective
 "Raise coverage of worldwide communities — local, sport, fraternal, union,
  international, traditional, net-native — explicitly including organizations
  that are probably not legally registered.

  READ 90-docs/community-coverage/iteration-runbook.edn FIRST and follow it
  exactly; it is the authoritative protocol and overrides any generic
  improve-the-repo instinct. This corpus is documentation, not code: add no
  tests, refactor nothing, and never touch manifest/west.yml — a correct
  iteration leaves it with a zero diff.

  One iteration: run the coverage reporter (default, regions, unpinned,
  integrity) and read the numbers; pick a gap, preferring the regions the
  reporter shows as thinnest, and grep the existing files to confirm the form
  is not already recorded; write ONE new community-orgs-<theme>-<n>.edn with
  4-6 entities in the exact attribute shape of the existing files; pin at least
  one entity to a real dated attributable source, and if the web is unreachable
  ship them unpinned as llm-recall-unverified rather than inventing a citation;
  rewrite the current-state block of ADR-2607257200 in place with the measured
  numbers; verify that integrity prints 'clean' and that edn-query still parses
  BEFORE committing; then commit, push the branch in its own command, and merge
  server-side with gh api merges. No rebase, no force-push.

  Invariants that matter more than throughput: never present a recalled number
  as a measurement; every entity states :org/member-count-basis including why
  it cannot be counted; reach, registrations, wallet addresses and cumulative
  memberships never go in :org/member-count but in :org/proxy-metric with their
  bias named; 'searched and not found' is a result worth recording; when two
  sources disagree keep the precise attributable one and record the
  disagreement rather than averaging; record harm and exclusion as part of the
  description; and where being counted is itself the hazard, record the form
  and do not seek rolls. A smaller honest iteration beats a larger one with a
  fabricated figure in it."
 :actor/capabilities #{:research :implementation :documentation}
 :actor/repository-visibility :private
 :actor/issue-authority :github-private
 :actor/hil-policy {:issue-create :autonomous
                    :patch-create :autonomous
                    :integrate :autonomous
                    :external-effect :approval-required}
 :actor/scale {:min 1 :desired 1 :max 1}
 :actor/runners [{:runner :claude :weight 3}
                 {:runner :claude-zai :weight 1}]}
